00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.440
How do we do that?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.250
We do that with two
basic platforms.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:12.530
We have our
Elastifile Cloud File

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.520
System, which is a
scale-out software only,

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.100
POSIX compliant file system.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.530
And we have
CloudConnect, which is

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:25.880
a system that allows you to
move the data into the cloud

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.780
and between a file
and an object layer.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:34.010
The Elastifile Cloud File
System is, as mentioned, POSIX

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:37.670
compliant, meaning you can
mount it as an NFS mount,

00:16:37.670 --> 00:16:42.200
as an SMB mount, to any
application that uses files.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.020
And what application
doesn't use files?

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:46.080
It's scalable.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.960
You can go to the
petabytes, you can

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:52.010
